'''''Begonia maculata''''' (''maculata'' meaning "spotted")<ref name="mac">{{cite web |title=A Grammatical Dictionary of Botanical Latin |url=https://www.mobot.org/mobot/latindict/keyDetail.aspx?keyWord=maculatus |website=www.mobot.org |access-date=8 July 2026}}</ref>, the '''polka dot begonia''',<ref>{{Cite web |last1=Kloß |first1=Julia |date=2020-06-26 |title=Forellenbegonie: Tipps für die pflegeleichte gepunktete Zimmerpflanze |url=https://utopia.de/ratgeber/forellenbegonie-tipps-fuer-die-pflegeleichte-gepunktete-zimmerpflanze |access-date=2021-05-03 |website=Utopia.de |language=de-DE}}</ref> is a species of begonia native to southeast Brazil.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2021-04-04 |title=''Begônia maculata'': conheça a planta tendência em decoração de interiores |url=https://revistacasaejardim.globo.com/Casa-e-Jardim/Paisagismo/Plantas/noticia/2021/04/begonia-maculata-conheca-planta-tendencia-em-decoracao-de-interiores.html |language=pt}}</ref><ref name=":0">{{Cite web |date=2019-10-22 |title=''Begonia Maculata'' Care - How To Grow Polka Dot Begonia |url=https://smartgardenguide.com/begonia-maculata-care/|access-date=2021-05-03 |website=Smart Garden Guide |language=en-US}}</ref> It grows naturally in the understory of the [[Atlantic Forest|Atlantic rainforest]], with occurrences confirmed in the Brazilian states of [[Espírito Santo]] and [[Rio de Janeiro (state)|Rio de Janeiro]].<ref>{{Cite web |last1=Jacques |first1=E. L. |last2=Gregório |first2=B. S. |date=2020 |title=''Begonia maculata'' |url=http://reflora.jbrj.gov.br/reflora/listaBrasil/FichaPublicaTaxonUC/FichaPublicaTaxonUC.do?id=FB5663 |access-date=2021-05-03 |website=Flora do Brasil |publisher=Jardim Botânico do Rio de Janeiro}}</ref> It has been introduced into Mexico, Cuba, the Dominican Republic, and Argentina.<ref name="105130-1" /> 

==Description==
''Begonia maculata'' has olive drab colored oblong leaves with silver dots. The undersides of the leaves are red-purple.<ref name="Lingfei">{{cite book |editor1-last=Li |editor1-first=Lingfei |editor2-last=Yang |editor2-first=Leilei |editor3-last=Ruihua |editor3-first=Ding |title=An Illustrated Book of Begonias |date=December 2023 |publisher=China Agricultural Press |location=Beijing |isbn=978-7-109-31617-1 |page=072-073 |edition=1 |ref=Lingfei}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=2021-05-03 |title=Točkasta begonija - ljepotica koja osvaja na prvi pogled |url=https://zena.rtl.hr/lifestyle/dom-i-interijeri/tockasta-begonija-ljepotica-koja-osvaja-na-prvi-pogled-f7dde70e-ab37-11eb-a48c-9a69ddd7a683 |access-date=2021-05-03 |website=Žena.hr |language=hr-HR |archive-date=2022-01-21 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220121145635/https://zena.rtl.hr/lifestyle/dom-i-interijeri/tockasta-begonija-ljepotica-koja-osvaja-na-prvi-pogled-f7dde70e-ab37-11eb-a48c-9a69ddd7a683 |url-status=dead }}</ref> The plant grows white or pink flowers in clusters with yellow centers on a single stem.<ref name=":0" /> 

==Taxonomy and history==
''B. maculata'' is placed under ''[[Begonia]]'' [[section (botany)|sect.]] ''[[Gaerdtia]]'', whose members are all mostly found in southern [[Brazil]]. Its [[sister taxa|closest relative]] is [[Begonia coccinea]].<ref name="DnC">{{cite journal |vauthors=Moonlight PW, Ardi WH, Padilla LA, Chung K, Fuller D, Girmansyah D, Hollands R, Jara-Muñoz A, Kiew R, Leong W, Liu Y, Mahardika A, Marasinghe LD, O'Connor M, Peng C, Pérez ÁJ, Phutthai T, Pullan M, Rajbhandary S, Reynel C, Rubite RR, Sang J, Scherberich D, Shui Y, Tebbitt MC, Thomas DC, Wilson HP, Zaini NH, Hughes M |year=2018| display-authors= 3 |title=Dividing and conquering the fastest-growing genus: Towards a natural sectional classification of the mega-diverse genus ''Begonia'' (Begoniaceae) |journal=[[Taxon (journal)|Taxon]] |volume=67 |issue=2 |pages=267–323 |doi=10.12705/672.3 |doi-access=free |url=https://www.researchgate.net/profile/Orlando-Jara-2/publication/325041923_Dividing_and_conquering_the_fastest-growing_genus_Towards_a_natural_sectional_classification_of_the_mega-diverse_genus_Begonia_Begoniaceae/links/5b02e8c2a6fdccf9e4f74c8c/Dividing-and-conquering-the-fastest-growing-genus-Towards-a-natural-sectional-classification-of-the-mega-diverse-genus-Begonia-Begoniaceae.pdf?origin=publication_detail&_tp=eyJjb250ZXh0Ijp7ImZpcnN0UGFnZSI6InB1YmxpY2F0aW9uIiwicGFnZSI6InB1YmxpY2F0aW9uRG93bmxvYWQiLCJwcmV2aW91c1BhZ2UiOiJwdWJsaWNhdGlvbiJ9fQ}}</ref>

